Three Things I learned through the Internet Fundamentals Intro activities are what an IP/ Geolocation Address is, Internet basics and how to use Git/Bitbucket. 
	First I learned what an IP address is and how it can be used to estimate where a device is located. I found my IPv4 address and checked if i had a IPv6 address as well. Then i used the Key CDN IP location finder to see what was linked to my own IP address. I saw that it can show general info like country, state, city or even approximate coordinates. It helped me understand how websites use location and data and how much privacy we actually have. 
	The tutorials on Git/bitbucket really helped too and showed me the basics of version control. I learned how to create a repo, save changes with commits, as well as mange files. It helped me create this repository and how to use it and store/share online code. 
	Before this class I never knew too much detail about the internet or how online connection works the internet basic tutorials helped me understand in depth about what it is and how it connects devices across the entire world. I also learned about different ways to connect to internet like WIFI, cable, DSI and satellite. This made me understand how data travels between devices and how it changes our everyday lives.
